2.43.0

Description: CVE-2026-86047 - Fix insufficient quoting in SHOW CREATE / mariadb-dump
 SHOW CREATE TABLE/USER/SERVER and mariadb-dump did not always quote or
 escape identifiers and values, so a low-privileged user could craft object
 names or option values that inject SQL into the dump/SHOW output, which is
 then executed when the dump is restored.
 .
 Backport of the five upstream MariaDB fixes (11.8.9) to 11.8.6:
  - MDEV-39818: InnoDB innobase_quote_identifier() now doubles embedded
    backticks (FK names in SHOW CREATE TABLE).
  - MDEV-39776: SHOW CREATE TABLE quotes/escapes all engine option values and
    rejects option names that are not plain identifiers; "*/" in values is
    escaped inside version comments.
  - MDEV-40308: SHOW CREATE USER / SHOW GRANTS escape single quotes in auth
    strings and TLS options and quote proxy user/host names.
  - MDEV-40311: mariadb-dump quotes trigger/plugin/UDF/server names and
    escapes SONAME, server wrapper/options and CHANGE MASTER values.
  - MDEV-40312: SHOW CREATE SERVER quotes the wrapper name and (non-legacy)
    option names. Historical keyword options (user, host, database, owner,
    password, socket, port) stay unquoted because the 11.8.6 grammar only
    recognises them as keywords; the CREATE SERVER grammar rework
    (09bc2533) is not part of this backport.
 .
 mariadb-dump in 11.8.6 is client/mysqldump.cc and dumps servers via
 SHOW CREATE SERVER, so the server name is now quoted in that statement.
 Test result files that could not be applied unmodified were hand-adapted to
 the 11.8.6 baseline.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/5acb43522863c9bd6b91f354104ea247bf513e9a, https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/d5d741a3076f911b468518d6b06a917593498c5b, https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/3646569225758c8225e7342783d775ef7c7570e5, https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/2b28d1c424104429eeed43115ee6d8a803671d52, https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/9d4ffe23b25808f7858b2dc48106fbd60cf0e513
