Description: CVE-2026-92262 - #mysql50# prefix mixes up table names in the table cache and on disk
 MDEV-40362: the legacy "#mysql50#" table/database name prefix was accepted
 on names that can be decoded from a file name into a regular table name,
 so `#mysql50#t1` and `t1` referred to the same file on disk but were
 different keys in the table definition cache. Now the prefix is only
 allowed on names that cannot be decoded from a file name, creation of new
 objects (tables, views, sequences, triggers, databases, partitions and
 subpartitions) with the prefix is rejected, and build_table_filename()
 returns an empty path for invalid names, with the callers checking for it.
 Backported from the 10.6 fix to the 11.8.6 code base: the name validation
 is ported to Lex_ident_fs::check_body(). Binary test fixtures and the
 partition upgrade sub-tests of the upstream main.upgrade test are not carried.
