Description: CVE-2026-97380 - GRANT PROXY with empty password incorrectly checks grantor's privileges
 MDEV-40470: an empty password and an empty plugin name do not mean
 "authentication was not specified", they mean "empty authentication was
 specified". LEX_USER::has_auth() treated an explicitly specified empty
 authentication (e.g. IDENTIFIED VIA '') as unspecified, so the check that
 the grantor has privileges on mysql.user was skipped. has_auth() now only
 checks whether an auth clause was present at all. The grammar already
 allocates USER_AUTH only when an IDENTIFIED clause is given in this
 version, so the corresponding sql_yacc.yy hunk of the upstream commit is
 not needed.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/dbd60d0ad8daa2d01050346aa50b7b102490e456
